, oversailing a recessed slatted base with wall lights on a lit plinth (00); west, a smaller rounded slatted pavilion raised on legs with a glass bay in its south face (00, 11); between them the long flat roof plane, timber soffit and pale edge, on dark posts, pierced by round oculi with palms through them (photos 01, 02, 05, 06, 12), over a lap pool running north-south with a little bridge (01) that runs out past the roof, and a pool that curves away north-west round a deck on piers, with a concrete coping, above a pond edged in rubble (02); a two-storey glass box on a timber deck, glass on its south face between dark mullions, slatted sides (08); and the north house of the night view (07): a concrete plinth with a raised pool edge, a glazed lit living room between concrete piers, a deep floor plate with an acrylic dome skylight, a glazed upper storey and a steel-framed glass room on the roof (07, 10), beside a rounded slatted tower. Palms (royal, coconut) and tropical understorey all round. Guessed: the plan and how the volumes join, their sizes (scaled from doors and storeys), every side not photographed, the roofs' tops, the oculi drawn as rough round holes, the number and placement of trees, the pond's extent. The house is placed only at Coconut Grove."}